<Layout title="About | GavDaly" description="About Gavin Daly and this website.">
  <Fragment slot="header"><h1>About Gavin Daly</h1></Fragment>
  <p>
    I’m Gavin Daly, a software developer based in Canada. I use this website to
    share the projects I build, technical notes I want to remember, and writing
    about the tools and ideas that shape my work. It is a personal site rather
    than a company or a product business, and the content reflects my own
    experiments and experience.
  </p>
  <p>
    My interests include privacy, security, efficient software, infrastructure,
    and sustainable computing. I enjoy working across the stack: designing a
    small interface, building a web application, configuring a home lab, or
    making the underlying system easier to understand and maintain. Current and
    past projects include Astro sites, Rust applications, Linux systems,
    networks, and experiments with self-hosted services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some projects here are complete and some are still in progress. I keep the
    unfinished work visible because the decisions, constraints, and lessons
    along the way are often more useful than a polished final result. You can
    browse the <a href="/projects">projects</a>, read the <a href="/posts">posts</a>,
    or <a href="/contact">contact me</a> with a question or comment.
  </p>
</Layout>
